    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n73778" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμοπαθ-ής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of the same feelings</i>
			or <i>affections, sympathetic,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕκαστος ἐν ταῖς ἀτυχίαις ἥδιστα
					πρὸς τοὺς ὁμοπαθεῖς ὀδύρεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Apollod.Com.
					8
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1161a26
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ. λύπης καὶ ἡδονῆς</span>
			<i>affected in the same way as others by</i> pain and pleasure,
				<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				464d
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[θάλαττα]</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Max.Tyr.
					39.5
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρῆμα ὁ. ἡμῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					15.1
				</span></i>
			.</div>
